    "narrative": "The LawDog engine identifies **Lawrence Butler** (70.35) and **Taylor Ward** (69.90) as our premier starts today. **Butler** benefits from a massive 13% boost via a favorable platoon matchup against Melton, while **Ward** and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) capitalize on a high-ceiling park environment against Rea. Despite Rea being a respectable arm, the park factors provide a significant lift to our outfield core. **Cal Raleigh** remains a top-tier play (65.29) as his power profile aligns perfectly with a soft matchup against Phillips. While **Tyler Freeman** (60.04) and **Gavin Sheets** (62.01) currently await confirmed lineup cards, their projections are bolstered by favorable SP xERAs (4.27 and 5.01, respectively), making them high-priority starts pending the final order confirmation.\n\nConversely, our toughest start is **Masyn Winn** (42.79), whose efficiency is suppressed by an elite matchup against Harrison; he remains in the lineup primarily to maintain our aggressive stolen base strategy, a recurring theme for this roster. The most difficult bench decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.14), who sits just outside the threshold for a start. While **Lee** provides steady contact, he was edged out by the superior power-projection of **Gavin Sheets** and the platoon upside of **Daulton Varsho**. We are keeping a close watch on **Bryce Harper**, who carries a high-variance profile today against a tough arm in Burns; while his score of 57.65 is respectable, his move to the leadoff spot provides enough OBP upside to justify his place in the lineup despite the challenging opponent.",
